            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2365676?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Local Network Access is a new permission which guards the use of local network adresses from a website, for example when trying to fetch 192.168.0.5 from a websites js code.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd really like to know implementation status across browsers for this.<br>\nThis is the spec:<br>\n<a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the blogpost for the chrome implementation<br>\n<a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/local-network-access\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/local-network-access</a></p>",
